1
00:00:07,910 --> 00:00:09,910
(Space Rice Cake)

2
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:13,590
(The saviour for the exhausted Earth Arcaders)

3
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:17,090
(Part-timer Gabee arrived.)

4
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:20,630
(Right from her first order, she radiated cheerful energy...)

5
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:24,960
(and showed off her cheeky, pleasant humour.)

6
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:29,170
(The customers fell for the part-timer's charm.)

7
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:31,199
(It's fun...)

8
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,140
(so far.)

9
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:35,439
(This one has only 2 shrimps...)

10
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,610
(whereas that one has 3 shrimps.)

11
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:38,980
(Starting with a complaint...)

12
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:40,510
(Please let there be 5 or more here.)

13
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:41,680
(Please let me see 5 or more when I lift this up.)

14
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:44,250
(They were running short on rice cake buns.)

15
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:46,220
(There's nowhere to fall back to.)

16
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:50,420
(Just when they thought things couldn't get any worse...)

17
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:53,990
(Clattering)

18
00:00:54,390 --> 00:00:57,730
(Yu Jin even dropped a burger on the floor.)

19
00:00:58,230 --> 00:01:03,230
(The dinner rush isn't going well. Could they wrap things up smoothly?)

20
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,740
They came out beautifully. They look so great.

21
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:07,009
(The 12 "Welsh Corgis" are finally good to go.)

22
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:08,610
I'm just naturally talented.

23
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:10,310
- Did you fall on the stairs? - Is this for real?

24
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,309
- No. I put one on the table first. - Yes.

25
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:13,609
I mean, I had two burgers on the tray.

26
00:01:13,610 --> 00:01:15,549
The moment I took one off, the tray lost its balance.

27
00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:16,550
- Oh, no. - Oh, boy.

28
00:01:16,551 --> 00:01:18,320
- The tray lost its balance. - I see.

29
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:20,320
I guess two burgers on a tray are all I can handle.

30
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:22,390
Right, Yu Jin. Be careful.

31
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:23,790
I'll make it quickly.

32
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:25,990
- Thank you. - Be sure not to get hurt.

33
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:27,889
By the way, I'm so happy...

34
00:01:27,890 --> 00:01:29,530
that Neapolitan Matfia said it was tasty.

35
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:32,799
- Exactly, Young Ji. You crushed it. - Yes, I did.

36
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,129
I wish he had ordered pizza and the other things...

37
00:01:34,130 --> 00:01:36,600
I wish he had tried your tteoksagna. It was really good.

38
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:38,070
- My point exactly. - Your tteoksagna.

39
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,669
(And meanwhile...)

40
00:01:40,670 --> 00:01:42,810
(Gabee is quietly getting her job done.)

41
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,679
- Gabee, are you doing all right? - Of course.

42
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:47,279
I'm doing great. I'm washing this right now.

43
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,349
- Thank you. - Don't mention it.

44
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:49,609
- I'm washing the dishcloth. - Thank you.

45
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:51,850
Don't worry. I love it.

46
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:53,789
I love my job.

47
00:01:53,790 --> 00:01:55,020
(She says the same phrases, but in a less cheerful tone.)

48
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,859
She's so sweet. She has such a good heart.

49
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:57,890
I know, right?

50
00:01:58,260 --> 00:01:59,819
She doesn't want to make us worry.

51
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:01,160
- She has such a fabulous mindset. - Right.

52
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,860
(Chuckling)

53
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:04,859
- Gabee, thank you so much. - Yes?

54
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,660
Don't mention it. This is fun.

55
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:08,099
Gabee, let's chant together. Ahk.

56
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,070
- Ahk. - Ahk.

57
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:12,800
- I don't know what that means. - You don't know what it means.

58
00:02:12,970 --> 00:02:14,239
- Let's go. - She's a total smile fairy.

59
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,440
(While the one with a "fabulous mindset" is doing a great job...)

60
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:18,539
There's a cutlery station upstairs.

61
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:19,639
You can take the cutlery there.

62
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,779
- And please put this on your table. - I see.

63
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:22,809
Thank you.

64
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:24,349
- One of it... - Yes.

65
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:25,520
- and 1 pomegranate ade. - And 1 pomegranate ade.

66
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:29,319
Table 11 ordered 1 original tteokbokki,

67
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,919
one pizza,

68
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:33,590
one shrimp burger, one beef burger,

69
00:02:33,730 --> 00:02:35,160
and one carrot cake.

70
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,559
And one extra pomegranate ade.

71
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,200
- We got a new order. - Okay.

72
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:42,099
One margarita, one ade,

73
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:44,139
one carrot cake, one pizza,

74
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:46,069
one tteokbokki, one shrimp burger,

75
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:47,839
- and one beef burger. - They're having everything.

76
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,840
- They're having one of everything. - They're having everything.

77
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,409
(Burger Status: 3 beef burgers including the 1 that dropped,)

78
00:02:52,410 --> 00:02:53,950
(three shrimp burgers)

79
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,480
I got the buns ready.

80
00:02:55,610 --> 00:02:57,280
- Take your time. - You're amazing as always.

81
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:01,420
(She cooks 3 patties at the same time.)

82
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:06,760
(Now that she's gotten a compliment from her master...)

83
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:09,890
(She presses the patty confidently.)

84
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:12,629
One shrimp burger is out.

85
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:14,799
- Three beef burgers. - Three shrimp burgers.

86
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,369
Two shrimp burgers, Mimi.

87
00:03:16,370 --> 00:03:17,470
Two more shrimp burgers.

88
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,439
Which shrimp burger came out?

89
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:21,539
- The one before the new order? - Yes.

90
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:23,510
- Then you have two to go now. - Okay.

91
00:03:23,610 --> 00:03:26,139
Our head chef is...

92
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:28,349
really good with numbers and has a good memory.

93
00:03:28,350 --> 00:03:30,679
- I'm upset with you, though. - Why?

94
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,120
You don't pay attention when new orders come in.

95
00:03:33,950 --> 00:03:35,120
That's not true. I do pay attention...

96
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:38,389
(Her inner thoughts she'd been bottling up burst out.)

97
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:39,719
- I'm sorry. - That's okay.

98
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,460
Relying on my own memory gives me peace of mind.

99
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:43,230
Thank you.

100
00:03:43,730 --> 00:03:46,630
A sous chef's job is to follow the head chef's orders.

101
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:48,299
I'm grateful for your existence.

102
00:03:48,300 --> 00:03:49,970
(Whenever she's upset, she reminds herself of their camaraderie.)

103
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:52,070
Cover these with basting domes, and we can play the shell game.

104
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,909
(The patties cooked with Young Ji's shell game skills...)

105
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:55,569
- Seriously. - Where is the shaker?

106
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:57,740
One beef burger is ready to replace the one Yu Jin dropped.

107
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:01,409
Here's a beef burger for the table that didn't get their order.

108
00:04:01,410 --> 00:04:02,410
Thank you.

109
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:05,649
- Be careful not to fall, princess. - Be careful.

110
00:04:05,650 --> 00:04:06,650
Thank you.

111
00:04:06,651 --> 00:04:08,749
It could happen because the floor is slippery.

112
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:11,120
- You guys are lifesavers. - You have two more to go.

113
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:15,230
(Fuelled by those cheerful words, she's back on server duty.)

114
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:17,759
- Here's your burger. - Already?

115
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,760
Thank you.

116
00:04:18,761 --> 00:04:20,429
- I'm sorry for the wait. - That's okay.

117
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:22,469
- It's okay. We'll enjoy this. - Please enjoy.

118
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:23,700
Thank you.

119
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,270
It looks good.

120
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,070
The cheese is melted to perfection.

121
00:04:28,170 --> 00:04:32,280
(The replacement burger satisfies the customer.)

122
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:34,050
- The burger is good. - Right.

123
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,649
(Burger Status: One beef burger, served,)

124
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:38,080
(one shrimp burger, served)

125
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,250
(Once the satisfied customers leave,)

126
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:44,060
(they get ready for a new customer.)

127
00:04:44,190 --> 00:04:45,620
It's still rewarding, isn't it?

128
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:47,590
- This is fun. - Indeed.

129
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:49,229
- You just keep going, you know. - Right.

130
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:51,200
(As they keep working on autopilot,)

131
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:55,869
(the dishes are piling up in the sink.)

132
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:57,040
What should I do with these?

133
00:04:58,540 --> 00:04:59,999
It's so great to have Gabee here.

134
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,170
- It's so great. - Indeed.

135
00:05:01,370 --> 00:05:03,010
Table 10 and Table 11.

136
00:05:03,370 --> 00:05:04,739
- Table 10 and Table 11. - I feel bad saying this,

137
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:05,939
but I'm just so happy.

138
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:06,979
Lee Young Ji...

139
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:08,079
(She's repeating the orders nonstop.)

140
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,250
Lee Young Ji for Table Ten.

141
00:05:09,710 --> 00:05:10,820
Lee Young Ji...

142
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:13,180
Lee Young Ji for Table 10 and Table 11.

143
00:05:13,750 --> 00:05:14,849
What about "Lee Young Ji?"

144
00:05:14,850 --> 00:05:16,520
Lee Young Ji for Table 10 and Table 11.

145
00:05:17,290 --> 00:05:18,890
Lee Young Ji for Table Ten.

146
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:20,790
A pomegranate ade for Table 11.

147
00:05:22,130 --> 00:05:24,600
(Talking to herself)

148
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,830
(For some reason, she just wants to say Young Ji's name.)

149
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:30,200
(Tell me more, tell me more)

150
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:33,670
(And for some reason, Gabee's labour song feels sad.)

151
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:35,439
(Singing)

152
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:39,110
They've actually been doing a messy job.

153
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:41,050
Who would work like this?

154
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:43,980
Who would put trash in the sink?

155
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:47,550
(It was you.)

156
00:05:48,490 --> 00:05:50,659
Goodness gracious.

157
00:05:50,660 --> 00:05:52,490
(She's giving herself an earful.)

158
00:05:52,560 --> 00:05:54,259
Two beef burger combos are ready.

159
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:56,690
One shrimp burger will be ready shortly.

160
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,699
(There's a beef burger on top, and the other one is a shrimp burger.)

161
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:01,029
- Two beef burger combos? - Two of beef and shrimp burgers...

162
00:06:01,030 --> 00:06:02,500
- will be out. - Oh, okay.

163
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:04,769
I'm sorry for speaking poorly.

164
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:05,869
- That's okay. - Don't be sorry.

165
00:06:05,870 --> 00:06:06,900
Don't say you're sorry.

166
00:06:07,410 --> 00:06:09,469
I need someone to complete the pizza.

167
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:10,510
I'll do that.

168
00:06:10,810 --> 00:06:12,310
What was I going to do?

169
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:15,110
(I'm here.)

170
00:06:15,550 --> 00:06:17,120
(Oh, the pizza!)

171
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:21,150
(The forgetful younger member...)

172
00:06:21,550 --> 00:06:24,790
(finished up the pizza.)

173
00:06:24,990 --> 00:06:26,560
The pizza is ready too.

174
00:06:28,460 --> 00:06:30,189
- I'm leaving. - See you later.

175
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:31,860
Here's the food.

176
00:06:32,730 --> 00:06:35,700
(Food keeps coming out miraculously despite everything.)

177
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:38,670
(The service team is picking up the pace.)

178
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:40,669
Here's your tteokbokki.

179
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:42,540
It's very hot, so I'll hold it for you.

180
00:06:42,910 --> 00:06:44,109
We need to cut this in smaller pieces.

181
00:06:44,110 --> 00:06:45,309
- It's too big. - I see.

182
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:47,680
Let's ask for a knife.

183
00:06:48,210 --> 00:06:50,209
- A knife? - I think we need one.

184
00:06:50,210 --> 00:06:52,249
- I'll cut it with the fork. - Do you need a knife?

185
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:53,419
Shall I bring you a knife?

186
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:55,649
- Can we get scissors, please? - Sure. I'll be right back.

187
00:06:55,650 --> 00:06:56,689
Thank you.

188
00:06:56,690 --> 00:06:58,390
(She smoothly jumped into their conversation.)

189
00:06:58,790 --> 00:07:00,459
We were supposed to give you these with the food.

190
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,189
- We forgot the tongs and scissors. - That's okay.

191
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:04,730
My sincere apologies.

192
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,500
Ye Na.

193
00:07:08,030 --> 00:07:09,100
Ms. Ye Na,

194
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:11,270
I'm deeply sorry about that.

195
00:07:13,470 --> 00:07:15,640
Could you please say you accept my apology?

196
00:07:16,010 --> 00:07:17,070
It's okay.

197
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:19,939
- Here you go. - Thank you.

198
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:20,950
Thank you.

199
00:07:21,350 --> 00:07:24,420
(While Eun Ji saves the day thanks to the child's generosity...)

200
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:27,119
You just have to keep moving and work fast.

201
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,550
Making good food takes a lot of hassle.

202
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:31,919
The more hassle, the better the food. It's such a hassle.

203
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:33,690
(It's a hassle?)

204
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:37,660
Director, it'll sting.

205
00:07:41,530 --> 00:07:43,970
Only a strong person like me can endure this.

206
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,440
Do you know what I'm afraid of?

207
00:07:47,370 --> 00:07:48,970
That one day, this will all feel easy.

208
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:55,250
(It may be a hassle, but the more effort you put in...)

209
00:07:55,810 --> 00:07:56,879
- Mimi. - Yes?

210
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,980
We're starting to run out of sauce bowls.

211
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,649
Sauce bowls? But I think that's...

212
00:08:01,650 --> 00:08:03,520
- Oh, those sauce bowls? - Yes.

213
00:08:04,090 --> 00:08:06,260
(The timing is perfect.)

214
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:09,060
- I washed these dishes. - Okay.

215
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:11,599
- Thank you so much. - She's incredible.

216
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:12,859
(A mountain of tableware arrived the moment Young Ji said it.)

217
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:13,969
She washed those at the perfect moment.

218
00:08:13,970 --> 00:08:16,900
- She's incredible. Shin Gabee. - Yes.

219
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:18,099
Shin Gabee.

220
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:20,570
Can someone please help me with the potatoes?

221
00:08:21,010 --> 00:08:22,040
I'll do that.

222
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:24,580
- Hello. - Oh, my.

223
00:08:24,780 --> 00:08:26,839
- Gabee, thank you so much. - I washed the dishes.

224
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:27,910
It's my job.

225
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:30,620
I'm impressed. Gabee works so fast.

226
00:08:31,350 --> 00:08:34,990
(Gabee, who works and moves fast,)

227
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:38,390
(restocks the self-service station.)

228
00:08:38,890 --> 00:08:42,390
(It seems that she's also quick-witted.)

229
00:08:42,590 --> 00:08:44,729
The bun came out great. Take a look at that.

230
00:08:44,730 --> 00:08:47,200
Nice. It's amazing. It's so easy to cut.

231
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,130
It's so easy to cut.

232
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:52,440
That's because it's hot.

233
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,310
It must be hard for you. The bun is really hot.

234
00:08:55,810 --> 00:08:58,180
- It's for a beef burger, right? - What do you mean?

235
00:08:58,280 --> 00:08:59,339
It's for a beef burger, right?

236
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:01,450
Well, Mi Hyun, I'm grateful.

237
00:09:01,610 --> 00:09:03,650
- I mean, it's for a beef burger. - Right.

238
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:05,850
What is she talking about?

239
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:07,989
(She got sentimental for a moment.)

240
00:09:07,990 --> 00:09:10,119
- Seriously... - It sounded like "pretty," right?

241
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:12,219
- I thought it was "happy." - "Happy?"

242
00:09:12,220 --> 00:09:13,489
- I thought she meant I was happy... - Right?

243
00:09:13,490 --> 00:09:14,760
because Gabee was helping us.

244
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:17,830
Why would I ask that when it's a given?

245
00:09:18,330 --> 00:09:20,629
Young Ji, where should I put this? Should I put it under here?

246
00:09:20,630 --> 00:09:21,630
Yes, please. My gosh.

247
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,099
- That's exactly what I needed. - Is that right?

248
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:25,939
- I'll bring more. I had no idea. - She's unbelievable.

249
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:26,969
She brought me a clean food pan.

250
00:09:26,970 --> 00:09:29,469
I wouldn't have been able to make any tteokbokki.

251
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:30,779
Oh, my. Unbelievable.

252
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:33,380
- Did she bring you a clean pot? - Yes, she did.

253
00:09:34,250 --> 00:09:36,309
- Shin Gabee. - Thank you.

254
00:09:36,310 --> 00:09:37,780
Gabee, what's the title of your new song?

255
00:09:38,450 --> 00:09:40,119
- It's "Bromm, Taki." - Come again?

256
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:42,250
- "Bromm, Taki." - It sounded like "running start."

257
00:09:42,990 --> 00:09:44,020
Can you say it again?

258
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:46,559
"Broom, Taki?" Oh, "Broom, Taki?"

259
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:49,460
- Yes, it's "Bromm, Taki." - "Broom, Taki."

260
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:52,429
- "Broom, Taki." - "Running Start" would be nice too.

261
00:09:52,430 --> 00:09:54,269
- "Running Start." - "Broom, Taki."

262
00:09:54,270 --> 00:09:56,730
(The kitchen is doing a running start.)

263
00:09:57,130 --> 00:09:59,240
Please put this on your table.

264
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:03,840
(The customers are walking upstairs.)

265
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,480
Hello.

266
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:10,849
Welcome to Space Rice Cake. Please take a table for two.

267
00:10:10,850 --> 00:10:12,520
(She told them to take a table for 2.)

268
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:16,620
(But...)

269
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:21,290
(All tables here are full.)

270
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:25,860
(There are no empty seats over there either.)

271
00:10:27,930 --> 00:10:30,970
(The only table left hasn't been cleared yet.)

272
00:10:32,670 --> 00:10:33,670
- No empty seats, right? - No.

273
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:37,270
- Thank you. - I'll bring them out in order.

274
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:39,340
- It'll take a while. - Okay.

275
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:41,750
(It's as if she foresaw the future.)

276
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:47,719
- Why haven't you sat down yet? - There are no tables left.

277
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,050
Really? A table for two?

278
00:10:49,550 --> 00:10:51,390
Give me a moment, please. I'll go check.

279
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:54,229
Hello, Table Two. You ordered...

280
00:10:54,230 --> 00:10:55,730
- a shrimp burger combo, right? - Yes.

281
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,799
You upgraded a soda to an ade, correct?

282
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:00,130
- Yes. - And...

283
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:02,599
- you ordered a margarita too, yes? - Yes.

284
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:04,900
Okay. We'll bring your food out as soon as it's ready.

285
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:07,099
- Take your time and enjoy the food. - Okay.

286
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:08,870
I'll bring you a glass of margarita.

287
00:11:10,010 --> 00:11:11,980
(Now she clears the empty table.)

288
00:11:12,710 --> 00:11:15,349
(She calls the customers when she's almost done.)

289
00:11:15,350 --> 00:11:16,380
Please come.

290
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:19,450
- I'm very sorry. - That's okay.

291
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:21,450
We're a bit busy today.

292
00:11:22,250 --> 00:11:24,259
- Did you order tteokbokki? - Yes, we did.

293
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,260
If you ordered tteokbokki,

294
00:11:27,490 --> 00:11:28,890
I'll leave this here.

295
00:11:30,030 --> 00:11:31,259
We need it to serve tteokbokki anyway.

296
00:11:31,260 --> 00:11:32,300
(She nails both efficiency and service quality.)

297
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:34,670
Oh, are you done?

298
00:11:36,870 --> 00:11:41,640
(The pizza master starts to communicate with the oven.)

299
00:11:42,110 --> 00:11:44,980
Can I bring out anything? Is the tteokbokki almost ready?

300
00:11:45,310 --> 00:11:46,940
- It'll be ready in three minutes. - The pizza is almost ready.

301
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,010
The pizza is coming out? Okay.

302
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:57,090
Because the dough is too thin...

303
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,760
- It looks messy. - Save the pretty buns.

304
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:04,499
It looks messy. I think we should make a new one.

305
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:07,330
(Reason for discarding: It's squished.)

306
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,069
- Take your time. No rush. - Right.

307
00:12:09,070 --> 00:12:11,100
- The dough is too thin, so... - Right.

308
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:13,339
I guess we shouldn't make it too thin.

309
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:15,640
Take your time. I'll do a better job next time.

310
00:12:16,210 --> 00:12:18,540
- It's okay. - You can do it.

311
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,340
I can do it.

312
00:12:20,910 --> 00:12:21,910
Hang in there just a little longer.

313
00:12:22,110 --> 00:12:25,450
(She desperately hoped for a good result, but...)

314
00:12:25,750 --> 00:12:29,590
(The second pizza is...)

315
00:12:34,490 --> 00:12:35,490
Please.

316
00:12:36,390 --> 00:12:39,059
- Please don't do this to me. - You can do it.

317
00:12:39,060 --> 00:12:40,060
We're almost there.

318
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,599
Oh, gosh. This is bad.

319
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,340
(The hardship came without any warning.)

320
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:48,540
(Reason for discarding: It's stuck to the tray.)

321
00:12:50,170 --> 00:12:51,710
Hold on. This is...

322
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:54,350
Why is the dough stuck here?

323
00:12:54,650 --> 00:12:56,210
- What? That's the villain. - Oh, no.

324
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:59,380
(Reason for discarding: Burnt dough)

325
00:12:59,650 --> 00:13:01,320
I did it. It's all my fault.

326
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:04,120
- No. I did it. I mean, it's... - I'll do a better job tomorrow.

327
00:13:04,590 --> 00:13:08,860
(As a matter of fact, hours ago...)

328
00:13:09,230 --> 00:13:12,560
(The ones with dark spots...)

329
00:13:13,930 --> 00:13:15,400
(Not bad?)

330
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,729
Is this 10mm thick?

331
00:13:16,730 --> 00:13:19,500
(They were gathered 1 by 1.)

332
00:13:19,670 --> 00:13:22,270
(It seems okay, so let's put it aside for now.)

333
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:25,810
(And their complacency...)

334
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,210
Oh, gosh. Wait. It's almost transparent.

335
00:13:29,750 --> 00:13:32,850
Your table number is seven. Please take this upstairs with you.

336
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:34,849
- We got a new order. - Got it.

337
00:13:34,850 --> 00:13:35,990
One beef burger,

338
00:13:36,590 --> 00:13:37,790
one pizza...

339
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:40,290
One pizza...

340
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:43,490
(Another pizza!)

341
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:45,730
I think we should stop taking pizza orders.

342
00:13:45,830 --> 00:13:48,100
- Let's stop taking pizza orders. - I'll let Eun Ji know.

343
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,830
This one looks... Is this okay?

344
00:13:51,570 --> 00:13:52,570
It doesn't look acceptable, right?

345
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:56,209
Don't take any pizza orders for now, okay?

346
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:57,370
- Oh, it's sold out? - Yes.

347
00:13:57,610 --> 00:13:59,910
Hello. May I take your order?

348
00:14:00,010 --> 00:14:02,350
Treat yourself to a big order.

349
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:04,850
- Can we order a lot? - No.

350
00:14:05,350 --> 00:14:06,780
I'm very sorry,

351
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:09,089
- but pizza is sold out. - Really?

352
00:14:09,090 --> 00:14:10,520
Yes. I'm sorry.

353
00:14:10,890 --> 00:14:13,059
We don't even have time to check our phones.

354
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,890
No, we don't. We're getting a total digital detox.

355
00:14:15,830 --> 00:14:17,489
Gabee, hang in there. We only have five tables left.

356
00:14:17,490 --> 00:14:19,029
I'll make you delicious tteokbokki.

357
00:14:19,030 --> 00:14:21,030
It's okay. I'm happy right now.

358
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:22,929
- You're lying. - I'm being honest.

359
00:14:22,930 --> 00:14:25,239
- It will be really delicious. - This is fun.

360
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,240
It will be really delicious.

361
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,570
You don't want to eat it anymore, do you?

362
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,840
This is fun.

363
00:14:31,610 --> 00:14:32,640
You're lying.

364
00:14:33,210 --> 00:14:34,210
You're a liar.

365
00:14:36,110 --> 00:14:37,750
- Goodbye. - That looks delicious.

366
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:42,319
(I'm already spoken for.)

367
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,120
It looks delicious.

368
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:47,730
Is this one ruined?

369
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:49,260
- Yes. - Oh, it's ruined.

370
00:14:49,460 --> 00:14:51,359
- You can eat it. - Then I'll eat it.

371
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:54,329
- Can you make an ade quickly? - Sure.

372
00:14:54,330 --> 00:14:55,770
(Startled)

373
00:14:56,130 --> 00:14:57,199
(Not even a moment of distraction is allowed.)

374
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,000
- We got a new order. - Okay.

375
00:15:01,410 --> 00:15:03,769
- Do we sell beer here? - Of course.

376
00:15:03,770 --> 00:15:04,809
(We understand how you feel, but we don't serve alcohol.)

377
00:15:04,810 --> 00:15:06,140
It goes perfectly with beer.

378
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,979
Bravo, bravo

379
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:12,250
(As a sad melody resonates through the kitchen,)

380
00:15:12,650 --> 00:15:15,520
(the pizza master finishes baking the last pizza of the day.)

381
00:15:16,650 --> 00:15:17,720
Please.

382
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,820
(It's squished.)

383
00:15:21,230 --> 00:15:22,290
Do you need any help?

384
00:15:23,260 --> 00:15:24,600
I think you can just flatten it out a little bit.

385
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:26,800
- It looks okay, right? Or not? - It looks okay.

386
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:29,070
- That shouldn't be served. - It's not good?

387
00:15:29,370 --> 00:15:30,670
- Is it bad? - It doesn't exactly look amazing.

388
00:15:31,070 --> 00:15:33,270
- But this is the last one. - Let's give them a refund.

389
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:35,210
(It's on the house.)

390
00:15:35,410 --> 00:15:37,109
- Let's make it on the house. - That'd be better.

391
00:15:37,110 --> 00:15:39,079
- It's a great idea, Chef Lee. - Right.

392
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,280
You're really good at this.

393
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:43,779
- Eun Ji taught me this. - That's a great idea.

394
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:45,120
(She learned this when she ruined Goguryeo Ramyeon in Goheung.)

395
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,749
Here's the pizza you ordered.

396
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:50,919
But since it didn't come out in the right shape,

397
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:53,859
the kitchen decided to give it to you on the house.

398
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:54,860
Thank you.

399
00:15:54,861 --> 00:15:56,990
- I'm sorry about that. - That's okay.

400
00:15:57,460 --> 00:15:59,430
It looks fine. Guys don't care about the looks.

401
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,429
It's okay. Let's dig in.

402
00:16:01,430 --> 00:16:02,800
(These customers are generous.)

403
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:06,140
(Even though it looks ugly, they take photos of it.)

404
00:16:06,570 --> 00:16:08,970
(He cuts a small piece and puts it in his mouth.)

405
00:16:09,110 --> 00:16:10,110
(Impressed)

406
00:16:10,510 --> 00:16:12,210
It's like a delicious pepperoni pizza...

407
00:16:12,410 --> 00:16:14,610
- A very spicy one. - with two drops of hot sauce.

408
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:18,780
(Fortunately, it seems like the pizza tastes good.)

409
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:20,420
Please insert your card.

410
00:16:22,450 --> 00:16:23,950
(Crowded)

411
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:26,490
Please put this on your table.

412
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:29,789
Hello. Let me take your order. May I have your name, please?

413
00:16:29,790 --> 00:16:31,329
- Gabee, could you please... - Yes?

414
00:16:31,330 --> 00:16:33,359
- read out the order for them first? - Read this?

415
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,929
- Okay. Oh, I'm sorry. - Here's the beef... I'm sorry.

416
00:16:34,930 --> 00:16:36,929
All right, let me read out the order.

417
00:16:36,930 --> 00:16:39,639
One ade, one margarita,

418
00:16:39,640 --> 00:16:40,840
one carrot cake,

419
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:43,870
one pizza, one tteokbokki,

420
00:16:44,410 --> 00:16:45,439
and one beef burger.

421
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:47,950
- We have no pizza left. - We don't have any pizza left.

422
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:50,310
Oh, no. Why did a pizza order come in?

423
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:52,980
- Oh, right. - You should cancel the pizza order.

424
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:57,250
(However...)

425
00:16:57,290 --> 00:16:59,159
- One original tteokbokki and pizza. - One pizza.

426
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:02,259
One ghost pepper pizza. This is very spicy.

427
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:03,959
- Thank you. - Thank you.

428
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,399
(Impatient Puppy forgot that it was sold out.)

429
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,900
- Why is there pizza? - I'll cancel it.

430
00:17:07,230 --> 00:17:09,100
- We have one more order. - Okay.

431
00:17:09,770 --> 00:17:11,339
Cancel pizza orders at two tables.

432
00:17:11,340 --> 00:17:12,670
(Yu Jin goes upstairs to sort things out.)

433
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:14,769
I'll cancel that order.

434
00:17:14,770 --> 00:17:15,970
This is for Table 12.

435
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:17,609
We're very sorry,

436
00:17:17,610 --> 00:17:19,440
but the pizza is sold out.

437
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:22,250
Would it be okay if we cancelled it?

438
00:17:22,550 --> 00:17:24,049
- The pizza is sold out. - I see.

439
00:17:24,050 --> 00:17:26,279
- Will it be okay if we cancel it? - That can't be helped.

440
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:27,480
Wait, what's this?

441
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:30,350
What's going on here?

442
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,419
What is this?

443
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:35,760
(The head chef tries to decipher the orders by herself.)

444
00:17:36,060 --> 00:17:38,500
(We have our first order!)

445
00:17:39,130 --> 00:17:45,670
(Those who are used to hearing Yu Jin read the menu)

446
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:53,040
(With the youngest one gone)

447
00:17:53,210 --> 00:17:54,779
- Beef burger and tteokbokki. - It went out.

448
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:56,449
- The original tteokbokki went out? - It went out.

449
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:58,449
- And one beef burger. - The beef burger is out.

450
00:17:58,450 --> 00:17:59,479
That's correct.

451
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:00,819
Did we make any mistakes?

452
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:03,090
(Writing is in black, and paper is white.)

453
00:18:03,490 --> 00:18:05,290
(Meanwhile...)

454
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:10,390
What's the matter?

455
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:13,530
Did you put basil mayonnaise instead?

456
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,069
- I did. - It's okay.

457
00:18:15,070 --> 00:18:16,070
It's okay.

458
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:17,839
Were you there?

459
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:18,899
(Another round of chaos)

460
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:20,640
Why didn't you tell me?

461
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:23,270
Director, you betrayed me.

462
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:25,779
- At Table 12... - Margarita.

463
00:18:25,780 --> 00:18:26,880
Table 12.

464
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:29,049
Eun Ji, you look very busy right now.

465
00:18:29,050 --> 00:18:30,579
A margarita at Table 12?

466
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:33,179
- Margarita for Table 8. - Margarita for Table 8.

467
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:35,720
- Margarita for Table 4. - Margarita for Table 4.

468
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:37,589
- As well as Table 6. - Let's serve Table 6 later.

469
00:18:37,590 --> 00:18:40,920
- One shrimp burger... - One more shrimp burger?

470
00:18:41,190 --> 00:18:42,459
I got it.

471
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:43,790
(Changing the order for the cancelled table)

472
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:46,459
- We have one more shrimp burger. - What?

473
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:47,799
One more shrimp burger.

474
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:48,929
- One more order of shrimp burger. - Okay.

475
00:18:48,930 --> 00:18:49,930
We have to make one more.

476
00:18:49,970 --> 00:18:51,699
(The last order: 3 tteokbokki,)

477
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:53,500
(3 beef burgers, 3 shrimp burgers)

478
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,340
We used all the rice cakes.

479
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:59,339
We sold a lot of tteokbokki today.

480
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:00,579
Business is booming today.

481
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:01,980
(It looks like they're getting closer to the 100,000-dollar dream.)

482
00:19:02,350 --> 00:19:05,580
(The floor manager who prepared a cheat sheet)

483
00:19:07,650 --> 00:19:14,390
(Performing her last dance with every ounce of her soul)

484
00:19:15,390 --> 00:19:18,700
(She pours out her soul.)

485
00:19:19,530 --> 00:19:22,430
(She adds a spoonful of performance.)

486
00:19:23,070 --> 00:19:24,969
(The margarita is ready.)

487
00:19:24,970 --> 00:19:26,840
Here are your beverages.

488
00:19:27,570 --> 00:19:29,939
- Thank you. - Thank you.

489
00:19:29,940 --> 00:19:31,280
(Thanks to the cheat sheet, she also finishes serving.)

490
00:19:31,410 --> 00:19:33,739
Yu Jin, is the shrimp burger for the table that ordered pizza?

491
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:35,149
(The youngest who was preparing the dessert)

492
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:36,150
That's right.

493
00:19:36,210 --> 00:19:37,950
One, two, three, four.

494
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:40,150
Four? Wait a minute.

495
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:42,250
One, two, three.

496
00:19:43,090 --> 00:19:45,690
(3 remaining carrots)

497
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:48,130
(However, 4 carrot cakes remain to be served.)

498
00:19:48,390 --> 00:19:50,790
(Unfortunately, she's short on 1.)

499
00:19:53,030 --> 00:19:55,270
There's something strange about the orders.

500
00:19:55,970 --> 00:19:57,269
- Yu Jin. - Yes?

501
00:19:57,270 --> 00:19:59,369
- I believe we have... - Yes.

502
00:19:59,370 --> 00:20:02,439
three more burgers to make.

503
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,639
- Isn't it 4 including... - I mean, 4.

504
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:05,909
- the shrimp burger I added earlier? - Yes.

505
00:20:05,910 --> 00:20:07,079
Right.

506
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,080
(Remaining burger orders)

507
00:20:08,081 --> 00:20:09,979
(This is what they have in mind.)

508
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:11,920
Should I go upstairs and check again?

509
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:13,979
- No, it's okay. - Is it okay?

510
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:14,989
It's okay.

511
00:20:14,990 --> 00:20:16,289
- Okay. - Thank you anyway.

512
00:20:16,290 --> 00:20:18,189
Gabee, you're already doing very well.

513
00:20:18,190 --> 00:20:19,190
(However...)

514
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:20,759
Can I take a photo of it?

515
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:21,889
(Table 4: 1 shrimp burger combo, 1 beef burger combo)

516
00:20:21,890 --> 00:20:23,389
(Table 8: 1 beef burger combo, 1 shrimp burger combo)

517
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:24,390
It's okay.

518
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:27,059
(Table 6: 1 beef burger combo, 1 shrimp burger combo)

519
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:29,299
(The actual number of burger orders)

520
00:20:29,300 --> 00:20:32,240
(1 beef burger and 1 shrimp burger are missing.)

521
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:36,070
(A total of 6)

522
00:20:37,010 --> 00:20:38,010
(The kitchen team has no idea either.)

523
00:20:38,011 --> 00:20:39,239
Mimi, I made two beef burgers.

524
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,740
- Okay. - One shrimp burger.

525
00:20:41,510 --> 00:20:43,509
(Yu Jin has no clue because she's busy with desserts.)

526
00:20:43,510 --> 00:20:45,350
One, two. I have to make one more.

527
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:48,390
Yes, I can do it.

528
00:20:48,650 --> 00:20:49,749
You can do it.

529
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:51,859
I just have to knead the dough and fry it now.

530
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:52,860
Let's go, Yu Jin.

531
00:20:52,861 --> 00:20:54,560
I won't allow any more cancellations.

532
00:20:55,930 --> 00:20:57,789
I can do it.

533
00:20:57,790 --> 00:21:00,460
(She decides to make more carrots.)

534
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,830
Yu Jin, give us a shout of "ahk."

535
00:21:04,270 --> 00:21:05,539
Ahk!

536
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:07,270
- All right. - Here it is.

537
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:09,740
Mimi, can I use one of the fryers?

538
00:21:10,170 --> 00:21:11,269
Which one?

539
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:13,379
- Can I use this fryer? - Sure.

540
00:21:13,380 --> 00:21:14,509
This or that.

541
00:21:14,510 --> 00:21:16,380
It's not off, is it?

542
00:21:19,450 --> 00:21:20,719
It's off.

543
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:22,749
(It's turned off.)

544
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:25,519
No one is helping me.

545
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:27,490
It's okay. You're doing very well.

546
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:29,529
Thank you for the compliment.

547
00:21:29,530 --> 00:21:32,130
(Frying the carrot rice cake until crispy)

548
00:21:32,530 --> 00:21:37,070
(Planting it quickly before it cools down)

549
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:40,399
- Here's your carrot cake. - Thank you.

550
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:41,709
One shrimp burger is ready.

551
00:21:41,710 --> 00:21:43,669
(The burgers start coming out.)

552
00:21:43,670 --> 00:21:46,439
Ta-da. Enjoy your food.

553
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:47,679
(Table 8: 1 original tteokbokki, 1 beef burger combo)

554
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:50,109
- This is the shrimp burger. - I see.

555
00:21:50,110 --> 00:21:51,110
(Even the sociable part-timer)

556
00:21:51,111 --> 00:21:53,019
- Yu Jin, I'll serve Table Eight. - Okay.

557
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:55,420
Erase the beef burger for Table Eight.

558
00:21:56,550 --> 00:22:00,320
Number 12 and 8.

559
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:04,629
Is there anything that hasn't come out yet?

560
00:22:04,630 --> 00:22:06,059
One shrimp burger is ready.

561
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:07,330
(They race toward the finish line.)

562
00:22:07,430 --> 00:22:09,130
- Beef. - Shrimp burger for Table Seven.

563
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:11,899
- Table 7. - Shrimp and beef for Table 7.

564
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:14,600
- These 2 are for Table 7. - Okay.

565
00:22:14,710 --> 00:22:17,139
(The part-timer goes to Table 7.)

566
00:22:17,140 --> 00:22:18,739
Hello.

567
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:20,179
You're Table Seven. Is this your order?

568
00:22:20,180 --> 00:22:22,549
- We never ordered it. - We got everything.

569
00:22:22,550 --> 00:22:23,580
- Really? - Yes.

570
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:24,880
That's strange.

571
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:27,319
(She retreats with an awkward laugh.)

572
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,320
Excuse me.

573
00:22:28,321 --> 00:22:30,290
Why are they making mistakes with us twice today?

574
00:22:31,020 --> 00:22:32,190
Listen.

575
00:22:33,060 --> 00:22:36,590
Table 7 already got 1 beef and 1 shrimp burger.

576
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:37,890
- Right? - Yes.

577
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,499
- It must be the one below. - Below?

578
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:40,500
- This one? - It's for this table.
Okay.

579
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:42,500
(She calls upon the power of collective intelligence again.)

580
00:22:42,501 --> 00:22:44,270
One beef burger for Table Six?

581
00:22:44,430 --> 00:22:46,240
- I'll also serve the shrimp burger. - Okay.

582
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:48,000
- Hello. - Hello.

583
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:52,010
Here's your shrimp burger.

584
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:54,279
And your beef burger.

585
00:22:54,280 --> 00:22:55,709
- Enjoy your food. - Thank you.

586
00:22:55,710 --> 00:22:56,710
Thank you.

587
00:22:57,310 --> 00:22:59,119
Eun Ji, how are things going upstairs?

588
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:00,749
- Absolute chaos. - Absolute chaos?

589
00:23:00,750 --> 00:23:01,750
Yes.

590
00:23:01,751 --> 00:23:03,419
What would we have done today without Gabee?

591
00:23:03,420 --> 00:23:04,820
- Exactly. - I know.

592
00:23:05,060 --> 00:23:07,720
It would've been a disaster without her.

593
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:09,989
(The part-timer is cleaning up,)

594
00:23:09,990 --> 00:23:11,500
(unaware of others talking about her.)

595
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:13,929
- How's the food? - We don't need...

596
00:23:13,930 --> 00:23:15,099
- It's very chewy. - Really?

597
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:16,569
We'll make you more right away.

598
00:23:16,570 --> 00:23:18,270
- Please wait a bit longer. - Okay.

599
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:20,699
(What's left behind after the good worker leaves)

600
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:22,240
- We must be the last customers. - That's fascinating.

601
00:23:23,340 --> 00:23:24,940
- There's no one else. - You're right.

602
00:23:25,110 --> 00:23:26,979
- We must be the last ones. - We should hurry.

603
00:23:26,980 --> 00:23:28,010
(A table with nothing but tteokbokki)

604
00:23:28,250 --> 00:23:29,780
Gabee, I'll make you some food.

605
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:32,419
- Are we really done now? - Yes.

606
00:23:32,420 --> 00:23:33,719
- We're almost done. - Are we?

607
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:35,790
We're done once the original tteokbokki is served.

608
00:23:35,990 --> 00:23:37,450
That's incredible. We're done.

609
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:39,919
One small original tteokbokki is ready.

610
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:41,219
(The tteokbokki they believe is their final order arrives.)

611
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:43,859
It's hot, so please don't touch it.

612
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:45,159
- Okay. - Thank you.

613
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:46,659
- Enjoy your food. - Thank you.

614
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:48,229
(Table 6: 1 mint carrot cake)

615
00:23:48,230 --> 00:23:51,270
Here's your carrot cake as well. Enjoy.

616
00:23:51,670 --> 00:23:52,899
Gabee, I'll make it delicious.

617
00:23:52,900 --> 00:23:54,969
Thank you. Are you making one for me too?

618
00:23:54,970 --> 00:23:56,770
I'll make it the best because I'll be eating it too.

619
00:23:57,370 --> 00:23:58,779
(Starting to make the staff meal that she promised)

620
00:23:58,780 --> 00:24:00,040
I'll make it the best.

621
00:24:01,780 --> 00:24:03,949
Hello. Did you enjoy your food?

622
00:24:03,950 --> 00:24:05,150
- Yes. - Yes.

623
00:24:05,750 --> 00:24:08,079
- Did you enjoy your food? - My goodness.

624
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,819
(Greeting the fans at the counter)

625
00:24:09,820 --> 00:24:11,490
Eun Ji, you worked so hard.

626
00:24:12,260 --> 00:24:13,790
You wrote the orders on yourself?

627
00:24:15,530 --> 00:24:16,659
It's making me emotional.

628
00:24:16,660 --> 00:24:19,159
It's going to make me cry.

629
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:20,730
(Tearing up at the orders tattooed on Eun Ji's arm)

630
00:24:21,230 --> 00:24:23,529
I feel bad for her.

631
00:24:23,530 --> 00:24:25,239
- Ye Seul. - Look at this.

632
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:26,700
I feel so bad about it.

633
00:24:27,700 --> 00:24:31,140
(In one corner of the dining area)

634
00:24:32,510 --> 00:24:35,809
(There's a table that's even more pitiful.)

635
00:24:35,810 --> 00:24:37,550
You want 1 beef burger and 1 shrimp burger?

636
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:39,679
All right, let's do it.

637
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:40,879
(She makes exactly the same as the forgotten order.)

638
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:42,419
Who wants to drink this?

639
00:24:42,420 --> 00:24:44,449
Who wants a pomegranate ade?

640
00:24:44,450 --> 00:24:45,759
Me.

641
00:24:45,760 --> 00:24:46,889
- That sounds good. - Please make one for me.

642
00:24:46,890 --> 00:24:47,960
I should make it.

643
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:49,189
The last pomegranate ades.

644
00:24:49,190 --> 00:24:50,529
(In a friendly atmosphere)

645
00:24:50,530 --> 00:24:52,329
I'll fry the fried food again.

646
00:24:52,330 --> 00:24:53,460
Of course.

647
00:24:54,330 --> 00:24:56,670
I'll give you this first.

648
00:24:57,070 --> 00:24:58,770
You're getting two burger combos.

649
00:24:59,500 --> 00:25:01,709
Gabee, feel free to take photos of this.

650
00:25:01,710 --> 00:25:03,140
Okay, I will.

651
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:04,809
- Gabee. - Yes?

652
00:25:04,810 --> 00:25:06,580
Please take a break and eat.

653
00:25:06,940 --> 00:25:08,980
I'll go upstairs and check.

654
00:25:09,650 --> 00:25:11,509
- Did you enjoy your food? - Could you check upstairs?

655
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:13,119
Yes, please be healthy.

656
00:25:13,120 --> 00:25:14,520
(Whether it's a blessing or a curse, the patrol begins.)

657
00:25:14,850 --> 00:25:16,990
Gosh, it looks delicious.

658
00:25:17,620 --> 00:25:19,319
Mimi, you worked so hard.

659
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:21,930
- How did you work so hard? - Gabee, you worked hard too.

660
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:23,160
(Signature menu items at Space Rice Cake)

661
00:25:23,161 --> 00:25:25,760
My goodness. It looks so good.

662
00:25:27,430 --> 00:25:30,900
(After working her tail off all day,)

663
00:25:31,330 --> 00:25:35,910
(the part-timer takes time to capture commemorative photos.)

664
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:37,739
(The head chef finally enters the dining area.)

665
00:25:37,740 --> 00:25:39,310
- Isn't it good? - Yes, it's good.

666
00:25:39,710 --> 00:25:41,140
- Hello. - Hello.

667
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:43,179
Hello, are you enjoying your food?

668
00:25:43,180 --> 00:25:44,679
- It's so good. - Hello.

669
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:45,680
(Going around to check on the customers)
- It's delicious. - We're about to close,

670
00:25:46,681 --> 00:25:47,880
so I came up to say hello.

671
00:25:48,650 --> 00:25:49,650
(And...)

672
00:25:49,651 --> 00:25:50,789
- Hello. - Hello.

673
00:25:50,790 --> 00:25:52,520
- Hello. - How was the food?

674
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:54,089
- It was really good. - It was delicious.

675
00:25:54,090 --> 00:25:56,129
- The fish... - The fish?

676
00:25:56,130 --> 00:25:57,829
- Wasn't it fried well? - Yes.

677
00:25:57,830 --> 00:25:59,359
I don't know who fried it. I can't wait for the burger.

678
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:00,560
It was Mimi.

679
00:26:00,730 --> 00:26:02,429
- What did you say? - I can't wait for the burger.

680
00:26:02,430 --> 00:26:04,969
You can't wait for the burger? What do you mean?

681
00:26:04,970 --> 00:26:07,300
Which burgers did you order?

682
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:09,039
- Here it is. - I'm just curious.

683
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:10,309
I've been making burgers nonstop.

684
00:26:10,310 --> 00:26:11,979
I'm just curious about your order.

685
00:26:11,980 --> 00:26:13,780
- I erased what we already got. - Beef and shrimp?

686
00:26:14,180 --> 00:26:15,810
(Rushing)

687
00:26:16,250 --> 00:26:19,480
(She suddenly bolts back toward the kitchen.)

688
00:26:19,620 --> 00:26:20,720
Freeze!

689
00:26:21,690 --> 00:26:23,620
- Freeze! - What's the matter?

690
00:26:23,990 --> 00:26:24,990
(Thankfully, freshly made burgers are still there.)

691
00:26:24,991 --> 00:26:26,990
What's the matter?

692
00:26:27,220 --> 00:26:29,129
(It's obvious that she made a mistake.)

693
00:26:29,130 --> 00:26:30,130
- Wait. - What is it?

694
00:26:30,131 --> 00:26:31,289
Freeze. Did you eat it already, Gabee?

695
00:26:31,290 --> 00:26:34,460
- No. - I'm sorry.

696
00:26:34,800 --> 00:26:37,170
- I didn't even touch it. - This isn't for you.

697
00:26:39,540 --> 00:26:42,109
We need tater tots.

698
00:26:42,110 --> 00:26:43,310
- Tater tots. - I thought...

699
00:26:43,840 --> 00:26:45,009
I thought that it was for me.

700
00:26:45,010 --> 00:26:46,909
- Which table is it? - Is it not for me?

701
00:26:46,910 --> 00:26:48,379
Can I give them these pomegranate ades?

702
00:26:48,380 --> 00:26:49,679
- Of course. - Three.

703
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:51,279
- Three? As an apology? - Three?

704
00:26:51,280 --> 00:26:52,319
There are three people.

705
00:26:52,320 --> 00:26:53,420
Wait.

706
00:26:54,180 --> 00:26:56,720
Right. That wasn't right.

707
00:26:56,990 --> 00:26:58,689
I'm sorry, Gabee

708
00:26:58,690 --> 00:27:00,120
- I'm really sorry - I knew it.

709
00:27:00,590 --> 00:27:03,489
(I'm sorry, Gabee. I'm really sorry)

710
00:27:03,490 --> 00:27:04,560
Take it upstairs.

711
00:27:05,030 --> 00:27:06,129
It was mine.

712
00:27:06,130 --> 00:27:07,159
(Feeling awkward, she scratches the back of her neck.)

713
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:08,200
Goodness.

714
00:27:08,830 --> 00:27:09,900
Goodbye.

715
00:27:10,070 --> 00:27:12,040
- I'm sorry, Gabee. - Bye.

716
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:15,170
- I'm really sorry. - I'm so sorry.

717
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:17,009
- It's okay. - We asked someone this talented...

718
00:27:17,010 --> 00:27:18,410
to do the dishes.

719
00:27:19,010 --> 00:27:21,980
(Meanwhile, the head chef who's carrying the tray carefully)

720
00:27:22,180 --> 00:27:23,850
How about some free pomegranate ade?

721
00:27:24,110 --> 00:27:25,379
- That sounds great. - That'd be great.

722
00:27:25,380 --> 00:27:26,550
Have some more.

723
00:27:27,250 --> 00:27:29,050
Even if you already ate, have some more.

724
00:27:29,290 --> 00:27:30,919
- I haven't eaten yet. - Please eat.

725
00:27:30,920 --> 00:27:32,320
Or you can drink all three.

726
00:27:33,220 --> 00:27:35,059
- It's really delicious. - You mean the burger?

727
00:27:35,060 --> 00:27:36,590
- It looks so good. - It looks delicious.

728
00:27:36,660 --> 00:27:38,699
I made the burgers too.

729
00:27:38,700 --> 00:27:39,999
- I knew it. - Is it lying down? Put it up.

730
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,169
It's tired because it's evening. Enjoy your food.

731
00:27:42,170 --> 00:27:43,370
- Thank you. - Thank you.

732
00:27:43,770 --> 00:27:46,640
(Taking a bite of the long-awaited burger)

733
00:27:46,840 --> 00:27:48,470
- The rice cake bun is good. - Yes.

734
00:27:49,270 --> 00:27:50,470
It doesn't taste like rice cakes.

735
00:27:50,670 --> 00:27:52,210
Which one is your favourite dish?

736
00:27:54,140 --> 00:27:55,180
The burger.

737
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:56,680
It's delicious.

738
00:27:57,210 --> 00:27:58,480
- Help yourself. - Okay.

739
00:27:59,250 --> 00:28:01,379
- I'll make an ade for myself. - Is there anything left?

740
00:28:01,380 --> 00:28:03,490
- I can have an ade, right? - Go ahead.

741
00:28:03,750 --> 00:28:04,790
Of course.

742
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:06,919
- I'll make one for you. - It's okay.

743
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:07,920
- Have a seat. - Gosh.

744
00:28:07,921 --> 00:28:09,629
- It's okay. - You're a customer.

745
00:28:09,630 --> 00:28:10,630
Don't worry.

746
00:28:10,631 --> 00:28:12,229
- There's no more ade anyway. - We feel so bad.

747
00:28:12,230 --> 00:28:13,700
No, it's okay.

748
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:17,000
There was a nice atmosphere when I was taking the photos.

749
00:28:17,770 --> 00:28:19,840
They looked quite good.

750
00:28:20,140 --> 00:28:21,469
Gosh, this is...

751
00:28:21,470 --> 00:28:23,709
- We even have two tteokbokki. - There are no buns.

752
00:28:23,710 --> 00:28:24,910
(There are no buns.)

753
00:28:25,310 --> 00:28:28,079
(The kitchen is in an embarrassing state.)

754
00:28:28,080 --> 00:28:29,150
I feel terrible for her.

755
00:28:30,510 --> 00:28:31,880
For the ade,

756
00:28:32,020 --> 00:28:34,419
there's no pulp at all, which is my favourite.

757
00:28:34,420 --> 00:28:35,489
Really?

758
00:28:35,490 --> 00:28:38,250
I'm making it only with juice, but it's okay.

759
00:28:38,820 --> 00:28:40,419
I'll be going home soon anyway.

760
00:28:40,420 --> 00:28:42,259
Excuse me.

761
00:28:42,260 --> 00:28:43,830
Has everything you ordered come out?

762
00:28:44,690 --> 00:28:45,929
Has everything you ordered come out?

763
00:28:45,930 --> 00:28:46,930
- Yes. - Gosh.

764
00:28:46,931 --> 00:28:47,959
I'm glad to hear that.

765
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:49,829
Has everything you ordered come out?

766
00:28:49,830 --> 00:28:50,830
- Yes. - We got everything.

767
00:28:50,831 --> 00:28:51,999
- You cleaned your plate. - Yes.

768
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,200
- Take your time. - Okay.

769
00:28:54,100 --> 00:28:56,209
- Did all your orders come out? - Yes.

770
00:28:56,210 --> 00:28:57,270
Thank you.

771
00:28:57,770 --> 00:29:01,380
(Back to the kitchen after checking every table)

772
00:29:01,950 --> 00:29:05,619
(Current time, 8:54pm)

773
00:29:05,620 --> 00:29:06,749
(Space Rice Cake)

774
00:29:06,750 --> 00:29:12,220
(Closed for business)

775
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:15,489
Young Ji, could you hurry and grill some meat?

776
00:29:15,490 --> 00:29:16,929
- The patties. - I'm ready to grill

777
00:29:16,930 --> 00:29:18,959
- Some meat - No, it's okay.

778
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:20,029
It's okay. I don't have to eat.

779
00:29:20,030 --> 00:29:22,229
You have to eat it.

780
00:29:22,230 --> 00:29:23,699
- Are you making it for me? - Of course.

781
00:29:23,700 --> 00:29:24,729
Really?

782
00:29:24,730 --> 00:29:26,669
How can you possibly hold back from eating it?

783
00:29:26,670 --> 00:29:28,399
I didn't think you were making it for me.

784
00:29:28,400 --> 00:29:29,409
That's a relief.

785
00:29:29,410 --> 00:29:32,110
(Starting with dishes that weren't snatched away)

786
00:29:32,180 --> 00:29:33,239
Gabee, let me get you a fork.

787
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:34,709
It's okay. You have to eat pizza with your hands.

788
00:29:34,710 --> 00:29:35,849
That's true.

789
00:29:35,850 --> 00:29:36,909
Use this, Gabee.

790
00:29:36,910 --> 00:29:39,019
- It's okay. - The dishes aren't done yet.

791
00:29:39,020 --> 00:29:40,949
Gabee, use this.

792
00:29:40,950 --> 00:29:41,990
Goodness.

793
00:29:42,750 --> 00:29:45,319
(A bite of tteokbokki with a toddler fork)

794
00:29:45,320 --> 00:29:47,059
(Humming)

795
00:29:47,060 --> 00:29:48,120
Isn't it good?

796
00:29:48,530 --> 00:29:50,429
It's not a place where people come...

797
00:29:50,430 --> 00:29:52,359
because it's run by Earth Arcaders.

798
00:29:52,360 --> 00:29:53,960
- You'd come for the food. - Right.

799
00:29:54,260 --> 00:29:55,670
That's what we wanted to hear.

800
00:29:56,370 --> 00:29:58,499
Wasn't today the busiest day we've had?

801
00:29:58,500 --> 00:29:59,800
- It was the busiest day. - Right.

802
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:01,870
- I bet we made a lot of money. - I should check the sales.

803
00:30:02,270 --> 00:30:03,569
- Could you tell us the sales... - I should take a look.

804
00:30:03,570 --> 00:30:05,010
while we make the burgers?

805
00:30:06,280 --> 00:30:08,009
(Gasping)

806
00:30:08,010 --> 00:30:08,790
Eun Ji.

807
00:30:09,910 --> 00:30:11,280
- Wait. - No way.

808
00:30:11,750 --> 00:30:13,050
Are they over 1,500 dollars?

809
00:30:13,150 --> 00:30:14,820
I'm not seeing it wrong, am I?

810
00:30:15,450 --> 00:30:17,319
- SK Hynix? - SK Hynix?

811
00:30:17,320 --> 00:30:18,520
We need to invest in SK Hynix.

812
00:30:18,827 --> 00:30:19,896
Two thousand?

813
00:30:19,990 --> 00:30:21,560
- Seriously? - Really?

814
00:30:21,620 --> 00:30:23,159
(Sales officially passed 2,000 dollars.)

815
00:30:23,160 --> 00:30:24,359
(33 beef burger combos, 17 shrimp burger combos,)

816
00:30:24,360 --> 00:30:25,599
(34 original tteokbokki, 20 ghost pepper pizza...)

817
00:30:25,600 --> 00:30:27,729
(Goguryeo Pizza, minus 22 dollars)

818
00:30:27,730 --> 00:30:30,130
(Total sales: 2,050.6 dollars)

819
00:30:30,300 --> 00:30:32,599
- Gosh, we made a lot. - Shin Gabee.

820
00:30:32,600 --> 00:30:34,940
- Let's go. - Shin Gabee.

821
00:30:35,570 --> 00:30:37,270
(Who am I?)

822
00:30:37,470 --> 00:30:39,339
- Shin Gabee. - Let's go.

823
00:30:39,340 --> 00:30:40,710
(The queen's name echoes through the kitchen.)

824
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:43,149
- Broom, Taki. - Let's go.

825
00:30:43,150 --> 00:30:44,479
Broom, Taki.

826
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:45,549
(Today's MVP returns the favour with a little dance.)

827
00:30:45,550 --> 00:30:48,080
- Thank you. - This is all thanks to Gabee.

828
00:30:48,890 --> 00:30:50,390
Gabee, try the shrimp burger first.

829
00:30:51,490 --> 00:30:52,989
(Meanwhile, a shrimp burger is made.)

830
00:30:52,990 --> 00:30:54,160
Zumba.

831
00:30:55,360 --> 00:30:56,430
I'll cut it for you.

832
00:30:56,560 --> 00:30:57,889
- In two minutes... - Are you wearing gloves?

833
00:30:57,890 --> 00:30:58,929
Yes.

834
00:30:58,930 --> 00:31:00,560
It tastes best when you eat it that way.

835
00:31:02,030 --> 00:31:04,100
Gabee, it's very hot.

836
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:09,869
- She's enjoying it. - It looks delicious.

837
00:31:09,870 --> 00:31:11,010
(Humming)

838
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:14,080
That's an American-style reaction.

839
00:31:14,440 --> 00:31:16,550
(Copying it immediately)

840
00:31:16,980 --> 00:31:18,449
(Exclaiming)

841
00:31:18,450 --> 00:31:20,680
- She's so kind and amazing. - An American-style reaction.

842
00:31:21,280 --> 00:31:23,049
The beef burger is coming. Wait a little.

843
00:31:23,050 --> 00:31:24,150
It's so good.

844
00:31:24,290 --> 00:31:25,720
I love basil.

845
00:31:26,320 --> 00:31:27,719
Most women like basil.

846
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:30,159
(As she likes it, she takes a big bite.)

847
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:31,330
Gosh.

848
00:31:31,490 --> 00:31:32,659
(The American girl's face says it all.)

849
00:31:32,660 --> 00:31:33,830
Young Ji.

850
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:36,100
That's American-style.

851
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:40,500
It's insane.

852
00:31:41,370 --> 00:31:42,809
- This tastes the best. - Yes.

853
00:31:42,810 --> 00:31:44,039
- I like this the best. - Is it your favourite?

854
00:31:44,040 --> 00:31:45,280
- Is it number one? - Is it your favourite?

855
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:46,939
- KARINA said the same thing. - It's number one.

856
00:31:46,940 --> 00:31:47,980
You're right.

857
00:31:48,140 --> 00:31:49,579
- Shall I pack it up for you? - It was so good.

858
00:31:49,580 --> 00:31:51,480
- Let's pack it for her. - Yes, please.

859
00:31:52,450 --> 00:31:53,479
I had fun.

860
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:54,579
Time went by faster...

861
00:31:54,580 --> 00:31:55,890
- than I expected. - Seriously.

862
00:31:56,090 --> 00:31:57,789
Out of all of us, you talked the most.

863
00:31:57,790 --> 00:31:59,289
- You were the most relaxed. - Seriously.

864
00:31:59,290 --> 00:32:01,460
- You changed the entire mood. - She really did.

865
00:32:02,630 --> 00:32:05,299
- You girls are so cute. - You worked so hard, Gabee.

866
00:32:05,300 --> 00:32:07,299
- No. - You were a big help.

867
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:08,359
We aren't just saying it.

868
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:10,069
- You were a huge help. - Really?

869
00:32:10,070 --> 00:32:11,730
- You helped out a lot. - I really enjoyed it.

870
00:32:12,300 --> 00:32:14,169
I loved it, Eun Ji.

871
00:32:14,170 --> 00:32:15,639
- Eun Ji... - How was it working here...

872
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:16,740
today?

873
00:32:17,770 --> 00:32:20,340
I realised that I enjoy watching it.

874
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:23,409
- That's exactly it. - I like the show so much.

875
00:32:23,410 --> 00:32:24,609
- Watching it is more fun. - I like the show so much...

876
00:32:24,610 --> 00:32:26,379
- that I prefer to watch it. - Right.

877
00:32:26,380 --> 00:32:27,749
- Gabee, I'll walk you out. - Okay.

878
00:32:27,750 --> 00:32:29,190
Get going.

879
00:32:29,620 --> 00:32:30,620
- It was so much fun. - Thank you.

880
00:32:30,621 --> 00:32:31,849
Well done, everyone.

881
00:32:31,850 --> 00:32:33,619
Congratulations on earning 2,000 dollars.

882
00:32:33,620 --> 00:32:34,689
It's all thanks to you.

883
00:32:34,690 --> 00:32:37,129
- It's thanks to you. - No way.

884
00:32:37,130 --> 00:32:38,900
- You must be so tired. - Shin Gabee.

885
00:32:39,030 --> 00:32:40,860
- Thank you. - Shin Gabee.

886
00:32:41,060 --> 00:32:42,369
- Goodbye. - Bye.

887
00:32:42,370 --> 00:32:43,969
I'll call you. Bye.

888
00:32:43,970 --> 00:32:45,469
- Bye. - Ahk.

889
00:32:45,470 --> 00:32:46,500
Ahk.

890
00:32:46,600 --> 00:32:49,510
(Leaving Space Rice Cake with a sense of relief)

891
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:53,010
(A commemorative selfie in front of the restaurant)

892
00:32:53,510 --> 00:32:56,780
(Just like that, our second part-timer left.)

893
00:32:57,150 --> 00:32:58,920
We earned 2,000 dollars in the evening.

894
00:32:59,650 --> 00:33:01,080
(Screaming)

895
00:33:01,680 --> 00:33:03,750
(It's time to celebrate breaking the 2,000-dollar mark.)

896
00:33:03,920 --> 00:33:05,990
(Congratulations)

897
00:33:06,590 --> 00:33:08,360
(Taking a moment to fully enjoy it)

898
00:33:08,860 --> 00:33:11,630
(An enthusiastic conductor and a balloon at the venue)

899
00:33:11,830 --> 00:33:14,030
(Umba)

900
00:33:14,530 --> 00:33:16,670
(Making sounds)

901
00:33:16,770 --> 00:33:18,530
(A perfectly synchronized quartet)

902
00:33:18,670 --> 00:33:23,369
(Singing)

903
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:25,069
- Dang. - Dang.

904
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:26,140
(Dang)

905
00:33:26,610 --> 00:33:28,179
Let's eat delicious food tomorrow.

906
00:33:28,180 --> 00:33:29,380
Our money...

907
00:33:31,210 --> 00:33:32,550
(Yareu)

908
00:33:32,720 --> 00:33:33,880
(Screaming with joy)

909
00:33:34,680 --> 00:33:37,190
(The head chef can barely contain the joy.)

910
00:33:37,420 --> 00:33:40,390
(Laughing triumphantly)

911
00:33:40,790 --> 00:33:42,860
(It's hard to tell how happy she is.)

912
00:33:43,290 --> 00:33:44,560
This is incredible.

913
00:33:44,660 --> 00:33:46,730
We can probably buy about three Hynix shares.

914
00:33:47,060 --> 00:33:49,230
The goal is to buy 4 shares and giving 1 to each of us.

915
00:33:51,130 --> 00:33:52,240
This is so cute.

916
00:33:52,500 --> 00:33:54,139
"Dear Earth Arcaders."

917
00:33:54,140 --> 00:33:55,170
(A handwritten letter from a customer)

918
00:33:55,570 --> 00:33:58,109
My child watched the show over 100 times.

919
00:33:58,110 --> 00:33:59,839
- Really? - She wrote you a letter.

920
00:33:59,840 --> 00:34:01,239
- My goodness. - Please read it.

921
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:02,950
Thank you so much.

922
00:34:03,180 --> 00:34:04,910
- We got a letter. - Read it out loud.

923
00:34:05,350 --> 00:34:08,419
"Hello, I'm "Earth Arcade" expert who watched the show..."

924
00:34:08,420 --> 00:34:10,389
"from Season 1 to 3 more than 100 times."

925
00:34:10,390 --> 00:34:11,749
"I'm ten-year-old Kwon Ye Na."

926
00:34:11,750 --> 00:34:12,890
"Earth Arcade" expert?

927
00:34:12,990 --> 00:34:14,359
"I watched it more than 100 times,"

928
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:16,090
"but it's still funny every single time."

929
00:34:16,460 --> 00:34:19,830
"To me, "Earth Arcade" is the funniest show."

930
00:34:19,900 --> 00:34:22,100
"It's the best variety show that I never get tired of."

931
00:34:22,670 --> 00:34:23,969
"Please don't let the season ever end."

932
00:34:23,970 --> 00:34:26,100
"Keep making it until I grow up."

933
00:34:26,270 --> 00:34:29,940
"So girls, please don't get sick and stay healthy."

934
00:34:30,370 --> 00:34:33,679
"Thank you for reading my letter all the way to the end."

935
00:34:33,680 --> 00:34:35,980
She told me not to get sick.

936
00:34:36,810 --> 00:34:39,019
- It hurts. - It's making me cry.

937
00:34:39,020 --> 00:34:40,320
(It's making me cry.)

938
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:41,850
Mimi, are you okay?

939
00:34:42,220 --> 00:34:44,550
- Are you crying? - Read this. It's so sad.

940
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:47,089
"Earth Arcade expert" is so cute.

941
00:34:47,090 --> 00:34:48,289
(A heartfelt letter melts away the exhaustion.)

942
00:34:48,290 --> 00:34:49,490
That's cute.

943
00:34:49,730 --> 00:34:51,589
Mimi, we worked so hard today.

944
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:53,100
Young Ji, you worked very hard.

945
00:34:54,100 --> 00:34:56,329
Everyone, well done today.

946
00:34:56,330 --> 00:34:57,330
Okay.

947
00:34:57,331 --> 00:34:59,140
- Today, - Our highest sales?

948
00:34:59,470 --> 00:35:00,899
- you hit another record. - Seriously.

949
00:35:00,900 --> 00:35:02,640
- Over 2,000 dollars. - We got the momentum.

950
00:35:03,140 --> 00:35:04,369
(We're happy but exhausted.)

951
00:35:04,370 --> 00:35:05,640
- And so... - And 50.5 dollars.

952
00:35:05,882 --> 00:35:09,352
Tomorrow morning, we have to fix the faucet...

953
00:35:09,377 --> 00:35:11,410
- I have to explain this. - What...

954
00:35:12,080 --> 00:35:14,580
(In the middle of the dinner service)

955
00:35:15,620 --> 00:35:17,550
- Gosh. - What's the matter?

956
00:35:17,950 --> 00:35:19,090
Are you okay?

957
00:35:19,860 --> 00:35:21,289
What happened?

958
00:35:21,290 --> 00:35:22,429
Let me explain.

959
00:35:22,430 --> 00:35:24,989
I went over to do the dishes.

960
00:35:24,990 --> 00:35:26,199
- Or whatever it was... - What were you doing?

961
00:35:26,200 --> 00:35:27,430
in the cooking process.

962
00:35:28,060 --> 00:35:31,099
You know how the faucet is always set to hot water?

963
00:35:31,100 --> 00:35:33,939
I had to turn it to cold. Or I would burn my hands.

964
00:35:33,940 --> 00:35:35,039
- Burn your hands? - And so,

965
00:35:35,040 --> 00:35:36,870
I turned it to the side like this.

966
00:35:36,940 --> 00:35:38,139
Then suddenly...

967
00:35:38,140 --> 00:35:39,480
- The faucet? - Yes.

968
00:35:39,610 --> 00:35:41,139
- The faucet? - If I turned it sideways,

969
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:43,680
how hard could I have possibly turned it?

970
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:45,349
It ended up like this.

971
00:35:45,350 --> 00:35:46,479
My first thought was,

972
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:48,990
"Someone must have broken it earlier."

973
00:35:49,490 --> 00:35:52,419
The point is, even if you want to prep tonight,

974
00:35:52,420 --> 00:35:55,089
you can't because of the faucet.

975
00:35:55,090 --> 00:35:56,929
- So you wanted to share good news. - To wash...

976
00:35:56,930 --> 00:35:59,799
You won't be able to wash anything.

977
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,729
So you should go home and recharge tonight.

978
00:36:01,730 --> 00:36:03,399
- Take a rest tonight. - We need to rest.

979
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,969
And...

980
00:36:04,970 --> 00:36:06,769
- come in tomorrow at 9:30am. - At 9:30am?

981
00:36:06,770 --> 00:36:07,770
- How about that? - Okay.

982
00:36:07,771 --> 00:36:09,809
Let's focus on our victory...

983
00:36:09,810 --> 00:36:11,939
- of earning 2,050 dollars. - Heart.

984
00:36:11,940 --> 00:36:13,209
Heart.

985
00:36:13,210 --> 00:36:14,610
Honesty, humility, ahk.

986
00:36:14,710 --> 00:36:16,050
(Congratulating themselves again)

987
00:36:16,150 --> 00:36:18,949
- Honesty, humility, ahk. - Honesty, humility, ahk.

988
00:36:18,950 --> 00:36:20,380
Please say it out loud.

989
00:36:21,750 --> 00:36:22,989
- Give us one little word. - She got me.

990
00:36:22,990 --> 00:36:24,889
- I was lip-syncing. - Give us one little word.

991
00:36:24,890 --> 00:36:26,219
- Honesty, humility, ahk. - Honesty, humility, ahk.

992
00:36:26,220 --> 00:36:27,660
(She got caught red-handed.)

993
00:36:27,760 --> 00:36:29,330
- Honesty, humility, ahk. - I'm so glad.

994
00:36:29,930 --> 00:36:32,029
It's over. Please go home.

995
00:36:32,030 --> 00:36:33,430
Please.

996
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:35,729
Director, please save me.

997
00:36:35,730 --> 00:36:37,929
- Get up. - I'm begging you.

998
00:36:37,930 --> 00:36:38,939
Please get up.

999
00:36:38,940 --> 00:36:42,069
How many times are you going to lie down here?

1000
00:36:42,070 --> 00:36:43,610
The floor is cold. Your mouth will freeze.

1001
00:36:44,270 --> 00:36:45,540
It'll be refreshing again.

1002
00:36:46,210 --> 00:36:47,610
Goodbye.

1003
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:50,249
Gosh, my feet.

1004
00:36:50,250 --> 00:36:53,250
We get off work and come in very regularly.

1005
00:36:53,380 --> 00:36:55,180
- Is this deja vu? - Seriously.

1006
00:36:55,590 --> 00:36:57,919
(They go home completely beat yet again today.)

1007
00:36:57,920 --> 00:36:59,590
Today was really exhausting.

1008
00:37:00,160 --> 00:37:03,190
- Out of all the seasons... - "Out of all?"

1009
00:37:03,430 --> 00:37:05,599
This is the only season which we didn't film a challenge.

1010
00:37:05,600 --> 00:37:07,099
- We didn't even dance. - We did dance a few times.

1011
00:37:07,100 --> 00:37:08,600
I have no new pictures of us in my phone gallery.

1012
00:37:09,400 --> 00:37:11,830
- I'm falling over. - Seriously.

1013
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:13,200
My body is slowly folding.

1014
00:37:13,870 --> 00:37:15,400
But I think I'm cut out for this.

1015
00:37:15,910 --> 00:37:17,369
- It's fun. As I said... - Yes.

1016
00:37:17,370 --> 00:37:18,370
- It's nice. - It's tiring but fun.

1017
00:37:18,371 --> 00:37:20,839
It's so tiring that I'm enjoying it.

1018
00:37:20,840 --> 00:37:23,710
- Really? - So it got rid of my evil side.

1019
00:37:23,810 --> 00:37:26,279
- You've reached enlightenment. - Evil, go away

1020
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:27,920
(Laughing)

1021
00:37:28,020 --> 00:37:30,489
- And I think I really love them. - The people?

1022
00:37:30,490 --> 00:37:31,950
- Cooking? - No, the three of you.

1023
00:37:32,190 --> 00:37:34,920
- Oh, my gosh, I'm so touched. - I'm dead serious.

1024
00:37:35,020 --> 00:37:36,589
- I really love you guys. - It's love.

1025
00:37:36,590 --> 00:37:37,930
I want to kiss you passionately.

1026
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:39,760
One after another.

1027
00:37:40,160 --> 00:37:42,570
- I don't fancy such a woman. - You don't?

1028
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:45,939
- Thank you for driving, Yu Jin. - Thank you.

1029
00:37:45,940 --> 00:37:47,000
(Anyway, she means she gets her energy from the members.)

1030
00:37:47,340 --> 00:37:50,310
- I want to check if she's sleeping. - Sexy and professional.

1031
00:37:51,170 --> 00:37:53,779
I didn't understand when people said your evil side would come out.

1032
00:37:53,780 --> 00:37:54,809
You feel it, don't you?

1033
00:37:54,810 --> 00:37:56,809
- Yu Jin was really busy today. - Yes, your evil side comes out...

1034
00:37:56,810 --> 00:37:57,879
when you're busy.

1035
